$\begin{align}
0.7^2 &= 0.7 \cdot 0.7
\\\\
&=0.49
\end{align}$

Since $0.7$ is seven tenths, we can use fractions instead:

$\begin{align}
0.7^2 &= \dfrac{7}{10} \cdot \dfrac{7}{10}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{7 \cdot 7}{10 \cdot 10}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{49}{100}
\\\\
&=0.49 &&\gray{\text{(Forty-nine hundredths)}}
\end{align}$
